{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Caleb silenced the people.</b> He silenced the people, who had already begun to raise their voices, as they did afterward, as it says: וַתִּשָּׂא כָּל הָעֵדָה וַיִּתְּנוּ אֶת קוֹלָם (Numbers 14:1)." "<b>Unto Moses.</b> So that they would hear what Moses would answer. And perhaps at that point Moses said what he afterward testified, saying: וָאֹמַר אֲלֵכֶם לֹא תַעַרְצוּן וְלֹא תִירְאוּן מֵהֶם (Deuteronomy 1:29), and Caleb reinforced his words by saying:" "<b>Let us go up.</b> It is fitting for us to go up, for they will not stand against us to prevent our ascent." "<b>And we shall possess it, for we are well able to do it.</b> For once we go up there, they will flee before us, for all the inhabitants of Canaan have already lost heart."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:42.290005367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}